generate-titles-in-resume-picker

Lane: frontend

Unit: manage-sessions-in-resume-picker

ChildPatch: generate-titles-in-resume-picker

Form: GitDiff

Segment: snapshot

Purpose: Manage saved sessions directly in the resume picker without entering a conversation.

Requires: FlatPatch:backend/persist-thread-settings-without-runtime

Provides: Independent recent-100-message titles using the highest-priority available luna-suffix model, manual picker naming, named digit profiles with themed hints and archive state for local sessions, restore-only actions, header progress and single-word title pinning. Ctrl+G admits the selected session to one FIFO queue while navigation and further admissions remain available, coalesces current and queued duplicates, exposes persistent target-aware activity and live progress, and dispatches at most one generation through completion and persistence. A cancellable two-second completion deadline applies even after the queue becomes idle; a failed target reports its error and the remaining queue continues, while picker closure discards unstarted work. Picker requests wait for native model completion without a separate 30-second cutoff.

Boundary: Native automatic titles and slash rename remain unchanged; backend persistence and rebuild recovery remain independent; picker actions submit no original-conversation model turn and preserve applied native effects on later failure; profiles support Embedded and LocalDaemon only. Only manually selected Ctrl+G targets are admitted; there is no private Alt+G bulk route, automatic list expansion, unloaded-page generation or global account lock.

Verification: Picker generation, catalog priority, missing luna, cancellation, naming, profile validation and persistence, themed footer wrapping, archive and restore, paging and pinning tests, plus native automatic-title and temporary-request tests. Controlled-completion tests verify repeated Ctrl+G admission during generation, persistent hints after navigation, FIFO target order, duplicate coalescing, serial dispatch, live progress, no unselected targets, stale completion rejection, continuation after a failed target and closure cancellation. Controlled native-client tests verify successful completion beyond 30 seconds, explicit cancellation and interruption on bounded temporary-turn timeout. Virtual-clock tests verify the complete two-second deadline, admission after idle time and cancellation during cooldown.


