+++ b/docs/resume-session-titles.md
@@ -0,0 +1,18 @@
+# Resume Session Titles
+
+- Explicit title generation in `codex resume` is independent of ordinary automatic TUI titles and `/rename` suggestions.
+- Generation summarizes the latest 100 nonempty user and assistant messages from native paginated history.
+- Assistant commentary is included.
+- Tool results and reasoning items are excluded.
+- The context prompt is bounded to 64 KiB and escapes conversation markup.
+- Generation selects the highest-priority available model whose name ends in `-luna`, including models hidden from the ordinary picker.
+- If no luna-suffix model is available, generation reports an error and preserves the saved name.
+- Generation uses low reasoning effort in an ephemeral, tool-disabled thread with the original conversation's model provider.
+- Picker generation follows the provider's native request timeouts and retries without a separate 30-second completion deadline.
+- Titles use lowercase English with at most ten words and have no fixed character limit.
+- Invalid output receives exactly one corrective request in the same ephemeral thread, retaining the original context and failed response.
+- Request failures do not trigger that semantic retry.
+- Title requests, outputs and usage are not persisted to session JSONL.
+- Local JSONL-derived usage totals therefore exclude these requests.
+- Generation does not add messages to the original conversation or change its model settings.
+- The saved name changes only after generation succeeds.
